---
import '../../styles/world-riso.css';
import Deck from '../../layouts/Deck.astro';
import RiceDeck from '../../components/RiceDeck.astro';

const contract = `IMPECCABLE DIRECTION CONTRACT — /rice/ · direction seed 3856f232 · mode: experience

THESIS: The rice writeup as the zine the scene actually prints. Refuses the dark
product-page frame; the machines are the ink, the frame is paper.

OWN-WORLD: Newsprint stock #EFE9DA, ink black #1A1A18, riso federal blue #3D5588,
fluorescent pink #FF48B0 — chosen because it rhymes with Cyberdream's #ff007c, so
the frame hands off into Act I rather than fighting it. Fira Sans Compressed 900
caps for display, Iosevka for all data, Fira Condensed for body. 2px ink rules,
halftone screen over every ground, registration marks at the plate corners, the
spine set as the zine's fold. Machine palettes unchanged.

STORY: A visitor reads a printed artifact about two machines, feels the press run
change ink at each act, and leaves knowing the discipline was engineering, not
decoration.

FIRST VIEWPORT: Even 50/50 fold. Heavy condensed caps break across the divider
with a second-ink misregistration; two machine plates below; the arrow-key
affordance set as a printer's registration mark.

FORM: split spine (surface seed 24fb6c50) inside direction candidate 7, assigned
by seed 3856f232. Grain and misregistration stay on grounds and illustration,
never under type — the subject is contrast rigor.

FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md`;
---
<Deck
  title="Two machines"
  description="Risograph-zine world for the /rice/ deck. Two desktop rices, each act printed in its own machine's inks."
  contract={contract}
>
  <RiceDeck />
</Deck>
